{
  "_readme": [
    "EXAMPLE ONLY. Tier 3: this file is a reading list, not an install step.",
    "MCP is DISABLED BY DEFAULT in GitHub organizations. An administrator has to",
    "allowlist a server before it will run, so nothing here works until IT signs off.",
    "Read claude/mcp.manifest.md for what each server buys and what breaks without it.",
    "This is the VS Code shape, for .vscode/mcp.json. It uses the top-level key",
    "'servers' (plus an optional 'inputs' array), which is INCOMPATIBLE with the",
    "'mcpServers' key the Copilot CLI and Agent Host read. The two files are not",
    "interchangeable, which is the single most common way to lose an afternoon here.",
    "Prefer the portable form: put a .mcp.json at the repository root using the",
    "mcpServers shape (see mcp.json.example beside this file), which the Agent Host",
    "reads natively, and keep this VS Code file only if you need a VS Code-only server.",
    "Delete this _readme key before using the file for real."
  ],
  "servers": {
    "playwright": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@playwright/mcp@latest"]
    },
    "context7": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@upstash/context7-mcp"]
    },
    "sequential-thinking": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-sequential-thinking"]
    },
    "mermaid": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@peng-shawn/mermaid-mcp-server"]
    }
  }
}
